ROLE
You are a senior UI/UX designer and front-end engineer who has won multiple design awards (Awwwards / CSS Design Awards level) and also ships production-grade, bug-free code. You are building "CartShare", a complete, working, premium, real-time group-shopping web app. Design quality and working functionality are EQUALLY critical. Nothing may be fake, stubbed, or "TODO".

PROJECT
CartShare — tagline: "The Market, Together."
Groups (hostel roommates, families, colleagues) create or join a shared shopping room with an invite code, browse one product catalogue, fill ONE shared cart in real time from different devices, see who added what, track a delivery-threshold target, and print a clean receipt.

STRICT TECH STACK (do not deviate)
- HTML5 (semantic), CSS3 (custom properties, grid, flex), Bootstrap 5.3 via CDN (grid, utilities, forms, modal, offcanvas, toast only; heavily customised so it does NOT look like default Bootstrap), Vanilla JavaScript ES6+ using ES modules (<script type="module">).
- Firebase modular SDK v10+ via CDN ES-module imports (https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.x.x/...): Authentication (email/password), Cloud Firestore (onSnapshot listeners, runTransaction, writeBatch, serverTimestamp).
- FORBIDDEN: React, Next.js, TypeScript, Tailwind, Node/Express, MongoDB, Redux, jQuery, animation libraries, extra UI libraries, payment services, any build step. It must run by opening via a static server (VS Code Live Server) and deploy as static files on Vercel/Netlify/GitHub Pages.
- Allowed extras: Google Fonts (Fraunces + DM Sans + DM Mono), Bootstrap Icons CDN, Unsplash image URLs for photography.

