SIGNATURE VISUAL LANGUAGE (use these to make it unique)
- Perforated "ticket" edges (CSS radial-gradient mask notches) on the basket slip, invite ticket and receipt.
- Ruled ledger lines (thin 1px --latte lines) as dividers instead of heavy cards; use cards sparingly. Prefer lists with hairline rules, numbered index labels (01, 02, 03) and asymmetric layouts.
- Rubber-stamp style badges (rotated -3deg, burgundy outline, mono uppercase) for states like "IN BASKET", "TARGET REACHED", "ROOM OPEN".
- Product catalogue called "The Stalls": a curated market board, with editorial product tiles (tall photo with slight arch or notched top, name in Fraunces, price in mono, category as small-caps label), NOT standard rounded e-commerce cards. Mix tile sizes subtly (featured tile spanning 2 columns every ~7 items) while keeping accessibility and scan-ability.
- Corners: mostly small radius (2–6px) or square; avoid pill-everything and avoid repetitive big rounded cards.
- Borders over shadows; if shadow is used, a single soft warm shadow.
- Motion (restrained, purposeful): hero headline staggered reveal, tile hover lift of 2–4px with image slow zoom, button press feedback, cart badge "bump" on add, changed cart row briefly highlights sage, Delivery Runway fills with eased transition, receipt slides up. NO continuous decorative animation, no cursor effects. Respect prefers-reduced-motion (disable all non-essential motion).
- Fully responsive: mobile-first. Desktop uses space efficiently. Mobile is deliberately redesigned (not just stacked): bottom sticky "Basket" bar showing item count + subtotal that opens the basket as a Bootstrap offcanvas bottom sheet; catalogue 2-column grid; category chips horizontally scrollable; activity feed in a collapsible section/tab. Touch targets ≥ 44px.
- Accessibility: semantic landmarks, labels on all inputs, aria-live="polite" for cart/activity/toast updates, visible focus rings (2px burgundy outline with offset), keyboard operable everything, alt text on images.

PAGE-BY-PAGE DESIGN
