2. FEATURES & EXACT BEHAVIOUR
═══════════════════════════════════════
Authentication: Firebase email/password. onAuthStateChanged guards every protected page (dashboard, room, join): if not signed in, redirect to login.html?redirect=<current url with params>. Redirect signed-in users away from login/register to dashboard. Persistence is Firebase default (browserLocalPersistence). On register: createUserWithEmailAndPassword → updateProfile(displayName) → setDoc users/{uid} {uid, displayName, email, createdAt: serverTimestamp()}. Never store passwords anywhere.

Room creation (rooms.js): generate code format "CS-" + 4 chars from "ABCDEFGHJKMNPQRSTUVWXYZ23456789" (no ambiguous 0/O/1/I/L). Use runTransaction: read roomCodes/{code}; if exists, retry with a new code (up to 8 attempts); else create atomically: roomCodes/{code} {roomId, roomName, status:'open', ownerUid, createdAt}, rooms/{roomId} {name, code, ownerUid, status:'open', threshold, deliveryCharge (default 40, ₹ charged only if subtotal < threshold and threshold > 0, clearly labelled configurable room setting), memberCount:1, subtotal:0, itemCount:0, createdAt, updatedAt}, rooms/{roomId}/members/{uid} {uid, displayName, role:'owner', joinedAt}, users/{uid}/rooms/{roomId} {roomId, name, code, role, joinedAt, lastOpenedAt}, plus a first activity doc "created the room". Use a pre-generated doc id (doc(collection(db,'rooms'))) so the transaction can set it.

Join (rooms.js): normalise code (trim, uppercase, auto-insert "CS-" if user typed only 4 chars, validate regex /^CS-[A-Z0-9]{4}$/). Read roomCodes/{code}; if missing → "We couldn't find a room with that code. Check it and try again."; if status != 'open' → "This room is closed." Then in a transaction/writeBatch: if members/{uid} exists → just navigate. Else create members/{uid} {role:'member'}, increment rooms/{roomId}.memberCount, create users/{uid}/rooms/{roomId}, add activity "joined the room". Navigate to room.html?room=<roomId>.

Shared cart data model: rooms/{roomId}/items/{productId} (the document ID IS the stable catalogue product id, e.g. "p_basmati_1kg", so duplicates are impossible by design) = { productId, name, unitPrice, image, category, totalQty, contributions: { [uid]: qty }, contributorNames: { [uid]: displayName }, updatedAt, lastUpdatedBy }. Product catalogue lives in js/products.js (≥ 36 products across 7+ categories: Fruits & Veg, Dairy & Eggs, Bakery, Pantry & Grains, Snacks, Beverages, Household & Care; realistic Indian prices in ₹, unit labels, Unsplash photo URLs; each with unique stable id). Provide a safe image fallback (onerror → a styled placeholder with product initial) so nothing ever shows a broken image.

Cart operations (cart.js) — EVERY write uses runTransaction that reads the item doc AND the room doc, recomputes values from the data, and writes both together:
 - addItem(product): if item doc missing → create with contributions {myUid:1}; else increment my contribution by 1 (this is Smart Merge: one consolidated line, show toast "Already in the shared cart — quantity updated." when the line already existed, otherwise "Added to shared cart"). totalQty = sum(contributions). Cap per-member quantity at 20 and reject invalid values.
 - changeMyQty(productId, delta): adjusts ONLY my entry; if it reaches 0 delete my key; if no contributions remain delete the item doc. Never touch other members' entries. Prevent negative or NaN.
 - removeMine(productId): remove only my contribution.
 - After each transaction recompute room.subtotal = Σ(item totalQty × unitPrice) and room.itemCount = Σ totalQty; to do this consistently, read all items inside the transaction (use a getDocs outside is NOT allowed for atomicity, so keep room.subtotal updated via delta: newSubtotal = oldSubtotal + (newLineTotal − oldLineTotal), clamp at ≥0) and ALSO have the client UI always compute displayed totals from the live items snapshot (single source of truth for display); room.subtotal/itemCount are denormalised only for the dashboard list.
 - Write an activity doc in the same transaction/batch: {type:'add'|'increase'|'decrease'|'remove'|'join'|'leave'|'create', actorUid, actorName, productId, productName, qty, createdAt: serverTimestamp()}. Activity must represent real actions only.
 - Disable the buttons while a write is pending, catch errors, show a toast on failure (e.g. permission denied, offline), never leave the UI stuck.

Real-time (sync.js): subscribe with onSnapshot to rooms/{roomId} (room settings/status), members, items, and activity (orderBy createdAt desc, limit 50). Handle metadata.hasPendingWrites with serverTimestamp null (show "just now"). On snapshot changes from OTHER users, briefly highlight changed lines (sage flash). Keep every unsubscribe function in an array and call them all on beforeunload/pagehide, on leaving the room, and on logout. If the room doc is deleted/closed or user is no longer a member, redirect to dashboard with a message. Show a small connection indicator (online/offline) using navigator.onLine events (real status, not fake "live users").

Delivery Runway (signature 1) — a horizontal track styled like a ruler/road with tick marks at 0, 25, 50, 75, 100% and a small basket marker that travels along the track toward a flag labelled with the target ₹ amount. Shows: current subtotal, target, remaining (max(0, target − subtotal)), percentage (min(100, …)). States: below → "₹120 more to reach the delivery target"; exactly/above → stamp "TARGET REACHED" and message "You've reached the ₹500 target." (do NOT claim delivery is free unless configured; copy: "Delivery charge waived under this room's rule" ONLY in the receipt logic where deliveryCharge is configured and subtotal ≥ threshold). If threshold = 0 show "No delivery target set". Add "Fits the gap" suggestions: up to 3 catalogue products with price ≤ remaining, preferring categories not yet in cart; each shows an "Add" button — NEVER auto-add. Animate bar width with CSS transition (transform/width), respecting reduced-motion.

Fair Share Ledger (signature 2) — ledger table: member avatar + name, items count, contributed value (₹), share of total (%) with a thin proportional bar in the member's colour. Top row: group subtotal. Footer row: sum of members = group subtotal (verify equality; computed from the same items snapshot using contributions × unitPrice). Include permanent small note: "Value of items each member added. This is not an amount owed." Members who left no longer appear in contributions because their contributions are removed on leave.

Smart Merge & Duplicate Guard (signature 3) — implemented through productId = item doc id; display "Smart Merge" confirmation toast + a small stamp "MERGED" shown on a line that has more than one contributor; each basket line expands to show per-member contributions.

Leaving/closing: member "Leave room" confirmation modal → transaction removes their contributions from all items (recompute line totals + room subtotal/itemCount), deletes members/{uid} and users/{uid}/rooms/{roomId}, decrements memberCount, logs "left the room". Owner cannot leave; owner can "Close room" (sets status 'closed' and roomCodes status 'closed'; members can still view the receipt but cannot modify the cart; UI shows a "CLOSED" stamp and disables add controls). 

Dashboard (dashboard.js): onSnapshot on users/{uid}/rooms, and for each room attach a listener to rooms/{roomId} to show live name/code/memberCount/subtotal/status (clean up listeners). Sort by lastOpenedAt desc. Update lastOpenedAt when entering a room.

Receipt (receipt.js): built from the CURRENT items snapshot at the moment of opening (re-render on every snapshot while the modal is open). Delivery charge logic: if threshold > 0 and subtotal > 0 and subtotal < threshold → deliveryCharge applied, else 0 and line shows "₹0 (target reached)" or "Not applicable". Final total = subtotal + delivery. Empty cart prints "No items in the basket yet". window.print() with css/print.css (@media print) as specified.

Validation & UX: every form validates (required fields, email regex, password length, matching passwords, room name length, threshold numeric/range), shows inline errors with aria-describedby, disables submit with spinner while loading, and shows success/error toasts (Bootstrap toast, styled). Escape ALL user-provided strings before inserting into innerHTML (write a tiny escapeHtml helper in js/utils.js) to prevent XSS. Format currency with Intl.NumberFormat('en-IN', {style:'currency', currency:'INR', maximumFractionDigits:0 or 2 as needed}); keep money in integers (rupees) or paise to avoid float errors.

